+"""Week-aware greedy scheduler (WFM-231), selected per client with `scheduler: week_aware`.
+
+Same template-placement idea as `greedy.py`, but the rules of the newer contracts are enforced while
+placing, against the agent's whole week, instead of being audited afterwards:
+
+  * rest: `min_rest_hours` of elapsed time between one shift's end and the next shift's start (both ways)
+  * split shifts only for the contracts in `split_shift_contracts`
+  * hour caps (elapsed), at most `max_consecutive_days`, skills, one shift per local day
+  * breaks: one per shift of `break.min_shift_hours` or more, started in the `break.window_hours` window
+    after the shift starts, in the planning interval with the largest gross coverage surplus
+    (agents on the queue ignoring breaks, minus required); ties go to the interval holding the fewest breaks
+
+Coverage is planned against the required curve *net of breaks*: after the first placement pass the
+breaks are placed by the rule above, intervals still short once breaks are taken out get another
+shift, and the breaks are re-placed, until no interval is short or no shift can be added.
+
+Deterministic: fixed template order, agent ids as the tie-break.
 """
